-25 | 2023-24 | 2022-23 | 2021-22 | 2020-21 |\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\n| Defined Benefit Obligations | 7052 | 5987 | 5048 | 4321 | 3544 |\\\n| Plan Assets | 5212 | 4518 | 4011 | 4037 | 3665 |\\\n| Surplus/(Deficit) | (1840) | (1470) | (1037) | (284) | 121 |\\\n| Experience adjustments on Plan assets | (34) | 61 | 35 | (275) | 79 |\\\n| Experience adjustments on Plan Liabilities | 1210 | 880 | 600 | 483 | 477 |\\\n\\\nAmounts for the current and previous four periods are as follows:\\\n\\\nMSKA & ASSOCIATES\\\nChartered Accountants\\\n\\\nStar Health And Allied Insurance Co. Ltd.\\\nCORPORATE\\\nOFFICE\\\nChennai-600 004\\\n\\\nTRCHA Chartered\\\n\\\nDHA & CO LLP\\\nAccountants\\\n\\\n* * *\\\n\\\nNotes to Financial Statements for the year ended 31 March 2025\\\n\\\n(All amounts are in Indian Rupees in lakhs, except for share data and where otherwise stated)\\\n\\\nC) Employee Stock Option plan (ESOP)\\\n\\\nThe Company has introduced Employee Stock Option plan (ESOP 2019) in the financial year 2019-20 effective from August 6, 2019 (date of grant). The Company has granted Stock Options to employees in compliance with the Securites and Exchange Board of India (Share Based Employee Benefits and Sweat Equity) Regulations 2021. The ESOP Plan 2019 was modified pursuant to the resolutions passed by the Board of Directors of the company in the meeting held on May 23, 2021, September 28, 2021 and January 25, 2022 and by the Shareholders of the Company in an extra ordinary general meeting held on July 16, 2021 , October 4, 2021 and March 03, 2022. Under the ESOP 2019, the company has given options to eligible employees to acquire equity share in the Company. The options have been granted under various tranches.\\\n\\\nDuring the year ended as at March 31,2025 the company had granted 3,51,679 No. of options (previous year: 5,76,000 Options) which will vest over a period of 5 years in the ratio 20:20:20:20:20 starting at the end of the $ ^{1} \\\\mathrm{st} $ year from the date of grant.\\\n\\\nOut of the ESOP 2019 options issued up-to the Year ended March 31, 2025:6,54,189 Options (Net of Withdrawn Option) (previous year: 6,90,989 Options), were issued for exercise price which is less than the fair value of the option. Therefore, the corresponding compensation cost of Rs.15 Lakhs (previous year: Rs.95 Lakhs) is charged to profit and loss accounts.\\\n\\\nMovement in the Options under ESOP:\\\n\\\n| Particulars | As at March 31,2025 | As at March 31,2024 |\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\n| Outstanding at the beginning of the year | 93,96,755 | 1,40,62,861 |\\\n| Add: Granted during the period | 3,51,679 | 5,76,000 |\\\n| Less: Forfeited / Lapsed during the period | 8,93,145 | 16,36,073 |\\\n| Less: Exercised during the period | 25,03,078 | 36,06,033 |\\\n| Outstanding at the end of the period | 63,52,211 | 93,96,755 |\\\n| Yet to be vested at the end of the period | 32,53,223 | 71,53,742 |\\\n| Yet to be exercised at the end of the period | 30,98,988 | 22,43,013 |\\\n\\\nFair Value method (Black Scholes method)\\\n\\\nThe fair value of options used to compute Pro-forma net profit/ (loss) and the earnings per Equity Share have been estimated on the date of the grant using Black-Scholes model.\\\n\\\n| Sl. No. | Particulars | As at March 31,2025 | As at March 31,2024 |\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\n| 1 | Annual Risk Free Interest Rate | 6.65% | 7.11% |\\\n| 2 | Expected Life | 5 Years | 5 Years |\\\n| 3 | Expected Annualized Volatility | 25.93% | 27.22% |\\\n| 4 | Dividend Yield | Nil | Nil |\\\n| 5 | Weighted Avg Price of the Underlying Share at the time of Option Grant (Rs.) | 470.54 | 382.41 |\\\n| 6 | Weighted Avg Fair Value of Options(Rs.) | 144.84 | 98.08 |\\\n\\\nThe key assumptions used in Black-Scholes model for calculating fair value as on the date of the grant are:\\\n\\\nStar Health And Allied Insurance Co. Ltd.\\\nCORPORATE\\\nOFFICE\\\nChennai-600 004\\\n\\\nTR CHADHA & CO LLP\\\nCHENNAI\\\nChartered Accountants