red Accountants\\\n\\\n* * *\\\n\\\nNotes to Financial Statements for the year ended 31 March 2025\\\n\\\n(All amounts are in Indian Rupees in lakhs, except for share data and where otherwise stated)\\\n\\\nDuring the year ended on March 31,2025 the Company has incurred interest on non-convertible debentures to the extent of Rs.4,093 Lakhs (previous year: 4,124 Lakhs).\\\n\\\n5.2.12 Amortization of premium / (Accretion of discount) on investments details are as follows:\\\n\\\n| Particulars | Year ended March 31,2025-Rs.in Lakhs | Year ended March 31,2024-Rs.in Lakhs |\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\n| Revenue Account |  |  |\\\n| Fire |  |  |\\\n| Marine |  |  |\\\n| Miscellaneous | 7,372 | 4,317 |\\\n| Profit & Loss Account |  |  |\\\n| Share Holders | 4,945 | 2,988 |\\\n| Total | 12,317 | 7,305 |\\\n\\\nAmortization of premium pertaining to revenue a/c and the profit & loss a/c have been adjusted against Interest, Dividend & Rent credited to the respective accounts.\\\n\\\n5.2.13 During the financial year under review, in respect of Expenses of Management, the company has not exceeded the sub segment limits prescribed under section 40C of The Insurance Act 1938, read with Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (Expenses of Management, including Commission, of Insurers) Regulations, 2024.\\\n\\\n5.2.14 Profit related Commission and Sitting fees paid to Non-Executive/Independent Directors:\\\n\\\nA) Profit related commission:\\\n\\\n| Name of the Director | Profit related Commission-Rs. in Lakhs |  |\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\n| Year ended March 31,2025 | Year ended March 31,2024 |  |\\\n| Mr.Rohit Bhasin | 25 | 25 |\\\n| Ms.Anisha Motwani | 25 | 25 |\\\n| Mr.Berjis Desai | - | 25 |\\\n| Mr.Rajeev Krishnamuralil Agarwal | 25 | 25 |\\\n| Mr.D.R.Kaarthikeyan | - | 10 |\\\n| Ms.Rajni Sekhri Sibal | 25 | 25 |\\\n| Mr.Rajeev Kher | 20 | - |\\\n\\\nB) Sitting Fees Paid:\\\n\\\nStar Health And Allied Insurance Co. Ltd\\\nCORPORATE\\\nOFFICE\\\nChennai-600 004\\\n\\\nTRCHA\\\nCharter\\\n\\\nADNA & CO LLP\\\nCHENNAI\\\nand Accountants\\\n\\\n* * *\\\n\\\nNotes to Financial Statements for the year ended 31 March 2025\\\n\\\n(All amounts are in Indian Rupees in lakhs, except for share data and where otherwise stated)\\\n\\\n| Name of the Director | Sitting Fees Paid-Rs. in Lakhs |  |\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\n| Year ended March 31,2025 | Year ended March 31,2024 |  |\\\n| Ms.Anisha Motwani | 33 | 30 |\\\n| Mr.Rajeev Krishnamuralilal Agarwal | 23 | 28 |\\\n| Ms.Rajni Sekhri Sibal | 23 | 28 |\\\n| Mr.Rajeev Kher | 17 | - |\\\n\\\n5.2.15 Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR)\\\n\\\nThe Gross amount required to be spent by the Company on CSR initiatives is Rs.372 Lakhs (previous year: Rs.NIL). The amount excess spent in the preceding 3 financial years is Rs.392 Lakhs.\\\n\\\nAs per the provisions of the Companies Act 2013, the excess spent amount shall be set off against the immediate succeeding 3 Financial Years. Accordingly, Rs. 372 Lakhs have been adjusted against the required to be spent and the Rs. 188 Lakhs (Rs 20 Lakhs of previous Financial Year and Rs. 168 Lakhs of Current Financial Year) have carried forward to next financial year for setting off as per the provisions.\\\n\\\nThe amount spent during the year is as follows:\\\n\\\n| S.No. | Particulars | Incurred and Paid For the year ended March 31,2025-Rs.in Lakhs | Incurred and Paid For the year ended March 31,2024-Rs.in Lakhs |\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\n| 1 | Construction / acquisition of any asset |  | - |\\\n| 2 | On purposes other than(1) above | 168 | 167 |\\\n\\\n5.2.16 The company does not have any long term contracts (other than long term insurance contracts) wherein the company is required to make provision towards any foreseeable losses.In respect of long-term insurance contracts, actuarial valuation of the liability as at March 31, 2025 is Rs. NIL (previous year: Rs.NIL ) There are no derivative contracts.\\\n\\\n5.2.17 The Indian Parliament had approved the Code on Social Security, 2020 which could impact the contributions by the Company towards Provident Fund and Gratuity.The Company will complete its evaluation once the Rules are notified and will give appropriate impact in the financial statements in the period in which the Code and related Rules becomes effective.\\\n\\\n5.2.18 Foreign currency exposure\\\n\\\nForeign currency exposure as at March 31,2025 and March 31,2024 that has not been hedged by any derivative instrument or otherwise is estimated as follows:\\\n\\\n| Particulars | Year ended March 31,2025-Rs. in Lakhs | Year ended March 31,2024-Rs. in Lakhs |\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\n| Foreign Currency Exposure on outstanding claims | 145 | 51 |\\\n| Reinsurance Accepted Outside India | 4,340 | - |\\\n\\\n* * *\\\n\\\nNotes to Financial Statements for the year ended 31 March 2025\\\n\\\n\\[All amounts are in Indian Rupees in lakhs, except for share data and where otherwise stated\\]\\\n\\\n5.2.19 Investor Education & Protection Fund:\\\n\\\nFor the year ended March 31,2025,the company has transferred Rs. NIL (previous year: Rs. NIL) to the Investor Education & Protection Fund.\\\n\\\n5.2.20 As per proviso to Rule 3(1) of the Companies (Accounts) Rules, 2014 which is applicable from April 1, 2023, the Company has used accounting software for maintaining its books of account, have a feature of recording audit trail (edit log) facility and the same has operated throughout the year for all relevant transactions recorded in the respective software. There are no instances of the audit trail feature being tampered with. The preservation of audit trail is as per statutory requirements for record retention effective from the financial year ended March 31, 2025.\\\n\\\n5.2.21 The Company has formed Steering committee of Department Heads to implement Indian Accounting Standards (Ind AS). The Steering committee meets regularly to discuss and take forward the implementation of Ind AS. The Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA) has issued Ind AS 117 (equivalent of IFRS 17) on August 12, 2024 but subsequently deferred its applicability vide MCA notification dated September 28, 2024 that Ind AS 117 will be applicable once it is notified by IRDAI.\\\n\\\nThe Company has engaged the knowledge partner and technology partner for Ind AS 117 implementations. \"Define 17\" System is implemented for convergence to Ind AS requirements. Data migration to Define 17 is completed. In addition to current IGAAP Financial Statements, the Company will be publishing Ind AS Compliant Financial Statements for the year ended March 31, 2025 along with previous year comparative numbers.\\\n\\\n5.2.22 No funds have been advanced or loaned or invested (either from borrowed funds or share premium or any other sources or kind of funds) by the Company to or in any other persons or entities, including foreign entities (\"Intermediaries\"), with the understanding, whether recorded in writing or otherwise, that the Intermediary shall, whether, directly or indirectly lend or invest in other persons or entities identified in any manner whatsoever by or on behalf of the Company (\"Ultimate Beneficiaries\") or provide any guarantee, security or the like on behalf of the Ultimate Beneficiaries.\\\n\\\n5.2.23 No funds have been received by the Company from any persons or entities, including foreign entities (\"Funding Parties\"), with the understanding, whether recorded in writing or otherwise, that the Company shall, whether directly or indirectly, lend or invest in other persons or entities identified in any manner whatsoever by or on behalf of the Funding Party (\"Ultimate Beneficiaries\") or provide any guarantee, security or the like on behalf of the Ultimate Beneficiaries.\\\n\\\nMSKA & ASSOCIATES\\\nConsulted Accountants\\\n\\\n5.2.24 Previous Year (PY) figures have been regrouped in the respective schedule and notes wherever necessary, to conform to current year groupings.The change has no effect on the statement of financial position:\\\n\\\n| Sr. No | Particulars (schedule and head of account) |  | Regrouped / Restated amount(Rs.In lakh) | Amount as per financials of previous year(Rs.In lakh) | Difference(Rs.In lakh) | Reason for regrouping/restatement |\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\n| Regrouped from | Regrouped to |  |  |  |  |  |\\\n| 1 | Sch3-Commission received on Re insurance ceded | Sch2-Re-insurance ceded to Claims paid | 38,476 | 37,878 | 598 | Presentation reclass based on nature of the income |\\\n\\\n* * *\\\n\\\nStar Health and Allied Insurance Co. Ltd.\\\n\\\nNotes to Financial Statements for the year ended 31 March 2025\\\n\\\n(All amounts are in Indian Rupees in lakhs, except for share data and where otherwise stated)\\\n\\\n| Sr. No | Particulars (schedule and head of account) |  | Regrouped / Restated amount(Rs. In lakh) | Amount as per financials of previous year(Rs. In lakh) | Difference(Rs. In lakh) | Reason for regrouping/restatement |\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\n| Regrouped from | Regrouped to |  |  |  |  |  |\\\n| 2 | Schedule 4-Operating Expenses | Form B-RA and Form B-PL(Interest, Dividend & Rent-(Gross)) | 2,39,356 | 2,39,442 | 99 | Presentation reclass based on nature of the expense |\\\n| Form B-RA(Towards remuneration of MD/CEO/WTD/Other KMPs) | -192 | As per the Master circular issued. |  |  |  |  |\\\n\\\nFor And On Behalf of Board of Directors\\\n\\\nArch\\\n\\\nStar Health and Allied Insurance Co. Ltd.\\\nSTAR\\\nCORPORATE\\\nOFFICE\\\n\\\n- Chennai-600 004 \\*\\\n\\\nAnand Roy\\\n\\\nManaging Director & Chief Executive Officer DIN: 08602245\\\n\\\nM.No.:138302\\\n\\\nP. Deepoh\\\n\\\nNilesh Kambli Chief Financial Officer\\\n\\\nDeepak Rami\\\nDirector\\\nDIN: 0763176\\\n\\\nneedi\\\n\\\n8\\\n\\\nJayashri\\\n\\\nSethuraman\\\n\\\nFor M SK A & Associates., Chartered Accountants Firm Reg No.: 105047W\\\n\\\nJayashree Sethuraman Company Secretary\\\n\\\nPlace: Chennai\\\n\\\nFor T R Chadha & Co LLP.