d on July 16, 2021, October 4, 2021 and March 03, 2022. Under the ESOP 2019, the company has given options to eligible employees to acquire equity share in the Company. The options have been granted under various tranches.\\\n\\\nDuring the year ended as at March 31,2025 the company had granted 3,51,679 No. of options (previous year: 5,76,000 Options) which will vest over a period of 5 years in the ratio 20:20:20:20:20 starting at the end of the 1st year from the date of grant.\\\n\\\nTR. QHADH\\\nchartered\\\n\\\nA & CO,LLP\\\ncontactinfo@a&co.com\\\n\\\nOut of the ESOP 2019 options issued up-to the Year ended March 31, 2025: 6,54,189 Options (Net of Withdrawn Option) (previous year: 6,90,989 Options), were Issued for exercise price which is less than the fair value of the option. Therefore, the corresponding compensation cost of Rs.58 Lakhs (previous year: Rs.81 Lakhs) is charged to profit and loss accounts.\\\n\\\nStar Health and Allied\\\n\\\nInsurance Co. Ltd.\\\nTAR\\\nnnai\\\n\\\n* * *\\\n\\\nESOP Scheme 2019:\\\n\\\n| Plan Period | Quantum of Grant | Method of Accounting | Exercise Period | Vesting Condition(s) | Grant Date | Grant/Exercise Price(Per Share) | Estimated Fair Value of share granted |\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\n| Series 1 | 1,71,31,339 | Black-Scholes Option Pricing model | 5 Years | 20% at 1st Anniversary from date of grant20% at 2nd Anniversary from date of grant20% at 3rd Anniversary from date of grant20% at 4th Anniversary from date of grant20% at 5th Anniversary from date of grant | 06-Aug-19 | 142.43 | 50.64 |\\\n| Series 2 | 2,47,229 | Black-Scholes Option Pricing model | 5 Years | 20% at 1st Anniversary from date of grant20% at 2nd Anniversary from date of grant20% at 3rd Anniversary from date of grant20% at 4th Anniversary from date of grant20% at 5th Anniversary from date of grant | 11-Jun-20 | 142.43 | 50.64 |\\\n| Series 3 | 50,000 | Black-Scholes Option Pricing model | 5 Years | 20% at 1st Anniversary f